  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a reference point for multimodal performance while reducing uncertainty about the core question: does combining RNA and image modalities (via simple concat fusion) yield meaningful accuracy over what single-modality baselines would achieve? config_011 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) is the lowest-cost multimodal configuration using standard, well-validated encoders. It avoids the expensive components (ViT-L, transformer aggregation, multiprofile, scgpt) that I want to reserve for later experiments once I know whether multimodal fusion is promising at all. If this baseline performs well, I can exploit by adding multiprofile/transformer/ViT-L; if it underperforms, I learn that the issue is architectural rather than modal. Expected relative cost: low — singleprofile, resnet50 (cheaper than ViT-L), no aggregation module, simple concat fusion make this the most budget-efficient multimodal test."
}

